- The x/y-swap strategy hits its 2500 cap too early, biasing toward small exponents
- Need more diverse B candidates including larger exponents for bigger lattices
- The tripling family and gap patterns should be expanded
- Need to ensure all lattices get good coverage, especially (6,12) and (12,6)

